# Cloudflare Pages Edge Rewrite Rules
# Per Part 11 §6 + challenge 1.2 — resolved for R2.
# The PDF galley local-looking URL (/journals/:initials/:slug/galley.pdf) is
# served by a Pages Function (functions/journals/[journal_initials]/[slug]/galley.pdf.ts)
# which streams the binary from the R2 bucket (binding GALLEYS) at the SAME URL.
# The frontend only renders the local-looking href; the edge proxy resolves it.
# The browser-crawler never leaves the same subdirectory (Part 10 Google Scholar
# rule satisfied), Git stays clean (no binaries tracked), and the download link
# gives instant PDF access from R2.

# --- Asset rewrites (200 proxy, NOT 301 — SEO-neutral, no redirect chain) ---
# Pages serves static files from dist/. With NO astro `base`, the pages live at
# dist/journals/* (matching the Worker's /journals/* fetches), but Astro emits
# ROOT-relative asset URLs (/assets/*, /favicon.svg, /_astro/*). The Worker
# fetches them as /journals/assets/* (address-bar origin amssr.org). These 200
# rewrites map /journals/assets/* back to the real /assets/* files so the
# styles/logos/favicon resolve under the proxy.
/journals/assets/*   /assets/:splat   200
/journals/_astro/*   /_astro/:splat   200
/journals/favicon.svg  /favicon.svg   200
/journals/favicon.ico  /favicon.ico   200
/journals/robots.txt   /robots.txt    200
